I invite Mr. Hannah to perform the same research.  The real cause of "loss
of jobs, destruction of culture, and personal alienation" during the time
of Ned Lud was the previously-enacted Enclosure Laws, a nasty little bit of
mercantilist Statism that forced the serfs out of their previous economic
niche.  The resulting influx of unskilled laborers to the cities (because
they had nowhere else to go), and the concomitant crowding, filth, and
squalor, coincided with the rise of industry, but was not caused by it. 
Rather, the other way around -- industry was able to grow more quickly by
drawing on this pool of cheap labor (which was created by Statist
interference).

Furthermore, during the communist era, "loss of jobs, destruction of
culture, and personal alienation" were the result not of
"industrialization" but of mercantilist State action (strike-busting cops,
for example) in collusion with SOME wealthy industrialists.  

